# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sluice frontend — copy to `.env` and adjust. `.env` is gitignored.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Origin the app sends API calls to. No trailing slash — route paths
# already start with /v1.
#
# DEV: point this at the Vite dev server itself, not the backend. Vite
# proxies /v1 to VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET below (see vite.config.ts), which
# makes every call same-origin and sidesteps CORS entirely.
#
# PROD: point it at the real backend origin, e.g.
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.sluice.example.com
# and set CORS_ORIGINS in the backend's env to this app's origin, or
# every request fails preflight.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5173

# Dev only — ignored by the production build. Where the Vite dev proxy
# forwards /v1. Must match the port the backend is actually listening on
# (docker-compose publishes 8008).
VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:8008

# Optional. Sent as `X-API-Key` only when non-empty.
#
# Note: this header cannot be attached to the SSE trace stream —
# EventSource sends no custom headers (see src/api/sse.ts). If that route
# ever requires auth it needs a cookie or a short-lived token, not this key.
VITE_API_KEY=

# Base delay for the trace-stream reconnect backoff, in milliseconds.
VITE_SSE_RECONNECT_MS=2000
